# Versions the offline bundle fetches. Sourced by script/offline_tools.sh, and
# overridable per call (KUBE_VERSION=v1.36.4 script/offline_tools.sh fetch).
#
# Keep these in step with the cluster you are building for -- kubeadm refuses
# to install a control plane more than one minor away from its own version.
KUBE_VERSION=${KUBE_VERSION:-v1.36.3}
# ⚠️ containerd 2.x needs glibc >= 2.34 -- Ubuntu 22.04+ or RHEL 9+. Measured
# on a CentOS 7 host (glibc 2.17): the binary will not start at all,
# "GLIBC_2.32 / GLIBC_2.34 not found". Drop to a 1.7.x build for older targets.
CONTAINERD_VERSION=${CONTAINERD_VERSION:-2.3.3}
RUNC_VERSION=${RUNC_VERSION:-v1.3.3}
CNI_PLUGINS_VERSION=${CNI_PLUGINS_VERSION:-v1.9.0}
HELM_VERSION=${HELM_VERSION:-v4.3.0}
HELMFILE_VERSION=${HELMFILE_VERSION:-1.8.0}
# crane, which moves images between a registry and a directory WITHOUT
# rewriting the manifest. `docker pull` picks one platform out of a multi-arch
# index and `docker save` stores that, so the digest a chart pins is gone
# before the bundle is carried anywhere -- measured on busybox:1.36, a 17-entry
# index that came back as a single manifest with a different digest. crane's
# OCI-layout round trip keeps it: same digest in, same digest out, and the
# image is still resolvable by the digest cilium's sixteen images pin.
# One static binary, like helm and helmfile.
CRANE_VERSION=${CRANE_VERSION:-v0.22.1}
# nerdctl, so step 2 can run the offline registry on a host with no docker:
# the install puts containerd in place, and nerdctl drives it directly. One
# static binary. It needs containerd >= 1.7 (older ones lack the streaming API
# nerdctl 2.x uses) -- the containerd above is 2.x; a registry host still on
# docker's bundled 1.6 keeps using docker.
NERDCTL_VERSION=${NERDCTL_VERSION:-2.4.0}

# Which platforms the bundle carries. One by default: a full multi-arch index
# is what a digest-pinned image needs, and what everything else pays for --
# pause:3.10 is 553 MB as an index and about 700 KB for one platform.
# Images the charts pin by digest keep their index regardless; this only
# governs the rest. A cluster with arm64 nodes wants
# BUNDLE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64,linux/arm64.
BUNDLE_PLATFORMS=${BUNDLE_PLATFORMS:-linux/amd64}

# helm-diff, the plugin `helmfile apply` and `helmfile diff` shell out to.
# `make helm-deps` installs it by cloning GitHub; a site with no outbound
# network gets it from here instead. The release tarball carries a built
# binary, so no compiler and no plugin hook are involved.
HELM_DIFF_VERSION=${HELM_DIFF_VERSION:-v3.15.13}
# The same major the pull-through caches in registry-mirror/ run (registry:3),
# so an install has one registry version to reason about rather than two.
REGISTRY_IMAGE=${REGISTRY_IMAGE:-registry:3}
# kubernetes/release tag the kubelet unit and the kubeadm drop-in come from.
# Those two files change rarely and independently of the kubelet version.
KUBE_RELEASE_TOOLS=${KUBE_RELEASE_TOOLS:-v0.16.5}
ARCH=${ARCH:-amd64}
